{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/18834","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:01.232906+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Handling it in the HIP impl sounds good - the HAL has a requirement that 0 workgroup count dispatches are ignored and this sounds like the right fix for that!","created_at":"2024-10-18T17:41:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/18834#issuecomment-2422949550","id":2422949550,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/18834","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M6Qa0au","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2422949550/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-10-18T17:41:50Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2422949550","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","id":75337,"login":"benvanik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"> Handling it in the HIP impl sounds good - the HAL has a requirement that 0 workgroup count dispatches are ignored and this sounds like the right fix for that!\n\nThanks @benvanik, I have that fix here https://github.com/iree-org/iree/pull/18835","created_at":"2024-10-18T17:43:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/18834#issuecomment-2422951135","id":2422951135,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/18834","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M6Qa0zf","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2422951135/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-10-18T17:43:00Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/2422951135","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10334089?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JamesMBartlett","id":10334089,"login":"JamesMBartlett","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzM0MDg5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JamesMBartlett","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### What happened?\n\nRunning a module with dynamic sized inputs on HIP fails when the input passed has a dynamic dimension with size zero.\n\n### Steps to reproduce your issue\n\n1. Compile a module with a dynamic input.\n<details>\n<summary>add.mlir</summary>\n\n```\nfunc.func @main(%input : tensor<?xf32>) -> (tensor<?xf32>) {\n  %result = arith.addf %input, %input : tensor<?xf32>\n  return %result : tensor<?xf32>\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n```\niree-compile --iree-hal-target-backends=rocm --iree-hip-target=gfx1100 --iree-hip-bc-dir=$(pwd)/bitcode add.mlir -o add.vmfb\n```\n\n2. Run the module with a zero-sized input:\n```\niree-run-module --device='hip://0' --module=add.vmfb --input='0xf32=1.1'\n```\n\n3. You should see an error like:\n```\nexternal/com_github_iree_org_iree/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/hip/event_semaphore.c:350: ABORTED; while calling import; while invoking native function hal.fence.await;\n[ 0] bytecode module.main:634 add.mlir:2:13\n      at add.mlir:1:1; invoking function 'main'; `sync func @main(%input0: tensor<?xf32>) -> (%output0: tensor<?xf32>)`\n```\n\nIf I make the following patch:\n<details> <summary>semaphore patch</summary>\n\n```\ndiff --git a/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/hip/event_semaphore.c b/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/hip/event_semaphore.c\nindex 926eb54ce5..7b2a30e9fb 100644\n--- a/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/hip/event_semaphore.c\n+++ b/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/hip/event_semaphore.c\n@@ -347,7 +347,8 @@ static iree_status_t iree_hal_hip_semaphore_wait(\n\n   iree_slim_mutex_lock(&semaphore->mutex);\n   if (semaphore->current_value == IREE_HAL_SEMAPHORE_FAILURE_VALUE) {\n-    status = iree_make_status(IREE_STATUS_ABORTED);\n+    status = iree_status_clone(semaphore->failure_status);\n+    //status = iree_make_status(IREE_STATUS_ABORTED);\n   }\n   iree_slim_mutex_unlock(&semaphore->mutex);\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\nThen I can see the actual error:\n```\nexternal/com_github_iree_org_iree/runtime/src/iree/hal/drivers/hip/stream_command_buffer.c:550: FAILED_PRECONDITION; HIP driver error 'hipErrorInvalidConfiguration' (9): invalid configuration argument; while invoking native function hal.fence.await; while calling import;\n[ 0] bytecode module.main:634 add.mlir:2:13\n      at add.mlir:1:1; invoking function 'main'; `sync func @main(%input0: tensor<?xf32>) -> (%output0: tensor<?xf32>)`\n```\n\nLooking into it more, one of the workgroup counts passed to `hipModuleLaunchKernel` on line 552 of stream_command_buffer.c, is zero which causes the invalid configuration error.\n\nI have a PR out that just skips kernel execution when any of the workgroup counts are zero, but let me know if you think this should be handled differently, for example somehow elliding the dispatch call from the compiler when the workgroup count is zero.\n\n\n### What component(s) does this issue relate to?\n\nRuntime\n\n### Version information\n\nrunning off of main as of October 17, 2024.\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_","closed_at":"2024-10-18T18:26:08Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","id":75337,"login":"benvanik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments":2,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/18834/comments","created_at":"2024-10-18T17:39:56Z","events